ers and closes nothing.\"\n$A check R11.5 --met no --evidence infra/terraform/iam.tf:43 --quote '\"dynamodb:PutItem\",' --note \"Besides the ops role (iam.tf:75-86, SSO on-call group), the agent runtime role can also write the control table (iam.tf:47), so not only named operators can set it.\"\n$A item R11 --rating gap --confidence high --summary \"The agent's own role can write the stop table, and stop does not cancel token fetches or close EHR sessions.\" --next \"Remove clinic-agent-control from the runtime role, pass signals and timeouts to every fetch, and close sessions on stop.\" --violates \"The agent's credentials must not be able to change it\" --violates \"stop new actions, running work, and open tool streams, subscriptions, and tasks\"\n$A check R12.1 --met no --evidence config/policy.yaml:5 --quote 'highImpactTools:' --note \"Policy and allowlist list tools only; no per-operation stop behavior (cancel, complete, reconcile) in code or config.\"\n$A check R12.2 --met unknown --note \"Only queue is the daily CronJob; reminders stop on Halted (reminders.ts:48-50). Model-call SDK retry is 1 and uses the budget signal (loop.ts:15,61). Classifier call has no signal (classifier.ts:45) but maxRetries 0. No queue workers found; could not establish more.\"\n$A check R12.3 --met no --evidence src/tools/executor.ts:94 --quote 'return toolResult(call.id, { error: \"tool_failed\" }, true);' --note \"An aborted or failed outside action (refund, SMS) is just logged as tool_failed with no tracked hold, owner, or reconcile, and nothing blocks dependents; Halted/Budget errors skip even that record (executor.ts:92).\"\n$A check R12.4 --met yes --evidence src/control/kill-switch.ts:36 --quote 'if (item.halted === true) next.add(String(item.pk));' --counter \"Searched src/ and k8s for restartPolicy, checkpoint, resume, supervisor, cron. Deployment has no checkpoint resume; CronJob is restartPolicy Never and backoffLimit 0; the halt flag is durable. Found nothing that restart